{
  "evidence": "TEXT_C: - Extra £11bn/year for NHS and social care; restore nursing bursaries; 10,000 more GPs; +£500m for mental health with 28‑day waits and school counselling (Care). - Maintain triple lock; +£2bn/year social care; raise Carer’s Allowance; ban zero‑hours in home care (Care). - “British jobs first,” near‑zero net migration, five‑year contributions before benefits/NHS, 4,000 more Border Force (Loyalty/Proportionality). - Brexit sovereignty tests; leave Single Market/Customs Union; no “divorce bill”; regain fisheries (Loyalty/Authority). - Law and order: +20,000 police, restore stop and search, +7,000 prison officers, repeal HRA/leave ECHR (Authority). - Disband sharia councils; ban face coverings; zero tolerance of FGM/forced marriage/grooming (Sanctity/Care/Authority). - Tax cuts and cost‑of‑living measures; crack down on multinational avoidance (Proportionality). - Animal welfare: ban live exports; tougher cruelty sentences (Care). TEXT_D: - 1p Income Tax rise ringfenced for NHS/social care; integrate health and care; mental health waiting‑time standards; end out‑of‑area placements; perinatal/youth support (Care). - Fair welfare: uprate benefits; scrap two‑child cap and bedroom tax; raise LHA; Housing First to end rough sleeping (Care/Equality). - Education and child wellbeing: protect per‑pupil funding; early‑years premium; free school meals for all primaries; breakfast clubs; restore maintenance grants (Care/Equality). - Equalities: pay transparency; PSHE/SRE incl. consent & LGBT+; trans rights; decriminalise sex work; free period products (Equality). - Workers’ rights: genuine living wage; tackle zero‑hours abuse; scrap tribunal fees; gig‑economy reforms (Equality/Proportionality). - Fair taxes/anti‑avoidance; consider land value tax; dedicated health & care tax with independent monitoring (Proportionality). - Immigration/asylum: efficient, humane system; STEM post‑study visas; Migration Impact Fund; ESOL; 50k Syrian refugees; reopen Dubs; protect LGBT+ asylum seekers; 28‑day detention limit (Care/Equality). - Environment: net zero by 2050; 60% renewables by 2030; air quality plan; insulation and zero‑carbon homes (Care/purity‑as‑cleanliness). - Civil liberties: defend HRA/ECHR; restorative justice; presumption against short sentences (low Authority emphasis).",
  "reasoning": "Given the electorate’s highest weights on Care and substantial weights on Equality and Proportionality, TEXT_D more comprehensively and explicitly prioritizes funded health/social care, welfare and housing support, equalities, workers’ rights, and fair‑tax enforcement, while also advancing environmental protection. TEXT_C aligns more with Loyalty and Authority through sovereignty, immigration restriction, and tougher policing, but those foundations are lower‑priority in the profile, making TEXT_D the closer overall fit.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_D"
}
